+## Curve
+CurveShape is a line of your own (a swoosh under a heading, an arrow pointing at a button, a divider, a wave, a sparkline): a CustomShape made for lines - open, stroked (Stroke.bEnabled true, Width 4, Round caps and joins), unfilled (bFill false), Self Hit Test Invisible. Path holds its points as box fractions (Contours[0].Vertices[i].Position, (0,0) top left, (1,1) bottom right; bClosed false). Smoothing: Smooth (Smooth Through Points - the curve flows through the points, Smoothness 0..2; a Disconnected vertex stays a sharp corner), Handles (each vertex's own InHandle / OutHandle), Straight (polyline, Corner Radius per vertex). Ends: StartMarker / EndMarker (None, Arrow, OpenArrow, Dot, Diamond, Bar) and MarkerSize (px) - they ride the ends of the Trim Path. Width: StartWidthScale / EndWidthScale (taper; 0 to a point), bUseWidthCurve + WidthCurve. bGradientAlongCurve (default true): a stroke gradient runs from the first point to the last. Draw it on: animate Trim End 0 -> 1 (Shape track TrimEnd). Ready-made curves: SetCurveFromTemplate (Line, Arc, SCurve, Wave, Zigzag, Spiral, Loop, Heartbeat, Swoosh, Bounce, Steps, Infinity) - or set Path directly. Curve Preset assets (WidgetCurvePresetAsset: Path, Smoothing, Smoothness, bApplyLook + the look): CurvePreset on a Curve applies and follows one. From Blueprint: SetPoints, AddPoint / AddPointAtLocalPosition (drawing), PlotValues (a chart of numbers), GetPointAtFraction / GetPointAtDistance (position + angle - move an icon along it), FindFractionNearest, GetCurveLength. Example spec: {class: "CurveShape", name: "Underline", props: {DesiredSize: {X: 240, Y: 24}, EndWidthScale: 0}}, then set_widget {widget: "Underline", props: {"Stroke.Paint.Color": "@accent"}} or set_shape_paint on its stroke.
